<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $899 mln September 4 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $899 mln September 4 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the seven major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $899 million to $41.448 billion in the week ended September 4, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $901 million to $41.685 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $2.828 billion to $734.135 billion.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
